    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n64859" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάλκιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάλκη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>freezing, benumbing</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιὼν</span> (sc. Mithridates) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάρμακον ἀσθενές τε καὶ μάλκιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόδε μοι μαλκίστατον ἦμαρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
				</span></i>
			<i>Fr.anon.</i><i><span class="en">
				45
			</span></i>:—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαλκιώτατον:
			μαλακώτατον</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαλκόν:
			μαλακόν</span>; the latter is cj. in Poet. ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				382
			</span></i>.</div>
